{
  "run_id": "PMC12991304__broad__web_text_chunks_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Conventional automotive exhaust catalysts use relatively high Pt or Pd loadings dispersed on supports such as TiO2.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Co-precipitating multiple metal cations can produce a homogeneous, single-phase high-entropy oxide matrix containing minimal PGM content.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The PGM content can be incorporated as isolated single atoms or alloyed into the high-entropy matrix.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10533845::web::027::discussion",
        "PMC10859931::web::012::structural_properties_of_n_pt_hea_c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A low-PGM high-entropy oxide catalyst will improve automotive exhaust catalytic activity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion",
        "PMC10533845::web::027::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A low-PGM high-entropy oxide catalyst will improve durability under automotive exhaust conditions.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion",
        "PMC8222268::web::019::structural_robustness_of_hea_nps",
        "PMC10533845::web::027::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed catalyst will reduce overall PGM consumption while retaining improved activity and durability.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High configurational entropy stabilizes a homogeneous structure and suppresses phase separation or secondary-phase formation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12933503::web::019::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-entropy structure suppresses catalyst sintering.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8222268::web::019::structural_robustness_of_hea_nps"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-entropy oxide structure promotes oxygen-vacancy formation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10533845::web::027::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Electronic interactions within the multimetal matrix optimize the d-band center of PGM sites.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10859931::web::012::structural_properties_of_n_pt_hea_c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sluggish diffusion in a high-entropy matrix helps preserve particle size and elemental dispersion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8222268::web::019::structural_robustness_of_hea_nps"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A heterogeneous mixture of metal cations increases active-site diversity and stability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion",
        "PMC12933503::web::019::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The diverse active sites facilitate reactant adsorption and oxygen dissociation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10859931::web::012::structural_properties_of_n_pt_hea_c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "D-band shifts at stabilized PGM sites lower effective reaction barriers and improve catalytic kinetics.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10859931::web::012::structural_properties_of_n_pt_hea_c",
        "PMC10533845::web::027::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed exhaust catalyst will achieve improved activity at lower overpotential.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12933503::web::019::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC10533845::web::027::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced mobility of PGM atoms will reduce sintering and deactivation under harsh operating conditions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8222268::web::019::structural_robustness_of_hea_nps",
        "PMC12933503::web::019::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to a conventional high-PGM Pt/Pd-on-TiO2 catalyst, the HEO catalyst will have a lower oxidation light-off temperature.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the conventional catalyst, the HEO catalyst will retain a greater percentage of its initial activity during prolonged operation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion",
        "PMC8222268::web::019::structural_robustness_of_hea_nps"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The benefits should persist under high-temperature, transient oxidizing and reducing automotive exhaust containing water vapor.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12005821::web::029::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
